''This article covers the Spanish moto driver named Julian Simon. For the American economist and author, who argued against Malthus and wrote about population and resources, see: [[Julian Lincoln Simon]]. 


'''Julian Simon''' (born in [[Villacanas]], [[Spain]], [[April 3]], [[1987]]) is a professional moto racer, height 167 cm, weight 56 kg. Team races: [[Honda]] (2002) [[Malaguti]] (2003), [[Aprilia]] (2004) &amp; [[KTM]] (2005). He has participated in 47 Moto Grand Prix; he won 1, in 2005, 125cc [[Great Britain Moto Grand Prix]]. 

{{Motorcycle-stub}}

