==Notes==
#{{note_label|backvocals|&amp;rsaquo;|none}}Soder can be heard singing background vocals on &quot;Forest Fire&quot; and &quot;Winnebago Warrior&quot; from the Dead Kennedys' album ''[[Plastic Surgery Disasters]]'', and playing synthesiser on &quot;Drug Me&quot; from the Dead Kennedys' ''Fresh Fruit For Rotting Vegetables''.
#{{note_label|trial|&amp;rsaquo;|none}}This was the first ever instance of a musician being put on trial for obscenity. Many sources cite the trial for [[2 Live Crew]] as the first, but that trial took place three years after Biafra's trial.
#{{note_label|assault|&amp;rsaquo;|none}}According to ''All Music Guide'', Biafra had both his legs broken from the attack.{{ref|huey3}} However, an issue of ''[[Rolling Stone]]'' claims that his injuries were &quot;extensive damage to the ligaments of one knee as well as a superficial head wound&quot;.{{ref|goldberg2}}
#{{note_label|influence|&amp;rsaquo;|none}}Biafra's spoken word work has been less influential to other artists than his music. However, Biafra's spoken word is often mentioned by [[Sean Kennedy]] as being a major influence on his work.{{ref|sktfmtv}}

